From 61e6038a3705fd2d0dbe5a93cfbbf0763fcc2140 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:03:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] external: build CLI11 without <codecvt> on libc++

CLI11's narrow()/widen() helpers use std::wstring_convert with
std::codecvt_utf8, which libc++ marks deprecated (both are removed in
C++26). The project compiles with -Werror, and -Wdeprecated-declarations
fires at the instantiation inside libc++'s own header, where CLI11's
diagnostic pragmas do not reach, so every translation unit that includes
CLI11 fails on macOS.

CLI11 already carries a wcsrtombs/mbsrtowcs fallback for compilers
without <codecvt>. Select it whenever libc++ is the standard library, by
_LIBCPP_VERSION, which the standard headers CLI11 includes first define.
The conversions produce the same strings.
---
 external/CLI/CLI11.hpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/external/CLI/CLI11.hpp b/external/CLI/CLI11.hpp
index 8a5b4c5..fce4cb2 100644
--- a/external/CLI/CLI11.hpp
+++ b/external/CLI/CLI11.hpp
@@ -160,6 +160,10 @@
 /** <codecvt> availability */
 #if defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__llvm__) && !defined(__INTEL_COMPILER) && __GNUC__ < 5
 #define CLI11_HAS_CODECVT 0
+#elif defined(_LIBCPP_VERSION)
+// libc++ deprecates std::wstring_convert and std::codecvt_utf8 (removed in C++26); under -Werror the use below fails.
+// CLI11 has a wcsrtombs/mbsrtowcs fallback that does the same work without them.
+#define CLI11_HAS_CODECVT 0
 #else
 #define CLI11_HAS_CODECVT 1
 #include <codecvt>
-- 
